{
  "name": "3 - Reply and Outcome Handler",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Sticky Note - s-setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 600,
        "height": 480,
        "color": 4,
        "content": "## THE STOP SWITCH\n\nThis is what stops the chasing. Without it the engine would keep nudging someone who has already written back, which is the single worst thing a follow-up system can do.\n\nIt watches the inbox. When an email arrives it checks whether the sender is someone with a live quote. If they are, the chase stops immediately and you get told.\n\n**Fill in before switching on:** the Airtable base/table IDs (`appREPLACE_...`), a token scoped to this base, and the owner email.\n\n**Order matters.** Switch this on BEFORE you switch on `2 - Chase Due Quotes`, never after."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Sticky Note - s-safe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        780,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 5,
        "content": "## Two ways to spot an opt-out\n\nGemini reads the reply and decides what it means.\n\n**If Gemini fails**, the workflow does not guess. It scans the text itself for the obvious opt-out words - unsubscribe, stop emailing, remove me - and if it finds any, it treats the reply as an opt-out.\n\nThe safety net errs towards stopping. Wrongly stopping a chase costs you one nudge. Wrongly continuing one after somebody asked you to stop is the thing that gets an email domain blocked."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Sticky Note - s-out",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1680,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 460,
        "height": 260,
        "color": 3,
        "content": "## What happens next\n\n**Opted out:** the record is flagged permanently. The engine filters on that flag, so they can never be picked up again - not by this quote, not by a future one.\n\n**Normal reply:** status becomes Replied and the next-due date is cleared, which takes it out of the engine's search. You get the reply forwarded so you can answer it like a human."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Watch the Inbox for Replies",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmailTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -120,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyHour"
            }
          ]
        },
        "simple": true,
        "filters": {},
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Normalize the Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.5,
      "position": [
        100,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "from_email",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ (($json.From || $json.from || '') + '').match(/[\\w.\\-+]+@[\\w.\\-]+\\.\\w+/)?.[0]?.toLowerCase() || '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "subject",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.Subject || $json.subject || '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "reply_text",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($json.snippet || $json.text || $json.textPlain || '') + '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a4",
              "name": "received_at",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Could Read a Sender Address?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        320,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ String($json.from_email) }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Ignore - No Sender",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        540,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "name": "Find a Matching Live Quote",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.airtable",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 2000,
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
      "position": [
        540,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "search",
        "base": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "appREPLACE_QUOTE_BASE",
          "cachedResultName": "Quote Follow-Up"
        },
        "table": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "tblREPLACE_QUOTES",
          "cachedResultName": "Quotes"
        },
        "filterByFormula": "=AND(LOWER({Client Email}) = '{{ $json.from_email }}', OR({Status} = 'Open', {Status} = 'Replied'))",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Alert Owner - Register Lookup Failed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 2000,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        540,
        380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "message",
        "operation": "send",
        "sendTo": "you@example.com",
        "subject": "Quote reply handler could not reach the register",
        "emailType": "text",
        "message": "=An email came in but the quote register could not be read, so the chase for this person may not have stopped.\n\nFrom: {{ $('Normalize the Reply').item.json.from_email }}\nSubject: {{ $('Normalize the Reply').item.json.subject }}\n\nWhat Airtable said: {{ JSON.stringify($json.error || $json) }}\n\nCheck this person by hand in the register - if they have a live quote, mark it Replied now so the engine does not nudge them again tomorrow.",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Is This About a Quote?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        780,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ String($json.id || '') }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Ignore - Not a Quote Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1000,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "name": "Gemini - Reply Reader",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "retryOnFail": false,
      "position": [
        920,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "modelName": "models/gemini-3-flash-preview",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Reply Reading Schema",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1100,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"intent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"One of: Interested, Not Interested, Question, Opt Out, Out Of Office, Unclear\"\n    },\n    \"is_opt_out\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The word true or the word false. true only if they asked not to be contacted again.\"\n    },\n    \"one_line_summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"One sentence, under 25 words, saying what they actually want.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"intent\",\n    \"is_opt_out\",\n    \"one_line_summary\"\n  ]\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Read the Reply",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 20000,
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
      "position": [
        1000,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Someone replied to a quote follow-up. Work out what they mean.\n\nFrom: {{ $('Normalize the Reply').item.json.from_email }}\nSubject: {{ $('Normalize the Reply').item.json.subject }}\n\nWhat they wrote:\n{{ $('Normalize the Reply').item.json.reply_text }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You read replies to quote follow-up emails for a small business and classify them. You never invent detail that is not in the message.\n\nPick the intent that actually fits:\n- Interested: they want to go ahead, or are close to it\n- Not Interested: they are declining this job\n- Question: they need something answered before deciding\n- Opt Out: they asked not to be emailed again\n- Out Of Office: an automatic away reply, not a real answer\n- Unclear: the message is empty, broken, or you genuinely cannot tell\n\nSet is_opt_out to the word true ONLY if they asked not to be contacted again. Declining this particular job is not an opt-out. When you are unsure, answer true - it is better to stop chasing someone who did not ask than to keep chasing someone who did."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Use AI Reading",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.5,
      "position": [
        1320,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "intent",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.output?.intent || $json.intent || 'Unclear' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "is_opt_out",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ String($json.output?.is_opt_out ?? $json.is_opt_out) === 'true' ? 'yes' : '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "summary",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.output?.one_line_summary || $json.one_line_summary || '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a4",
              "name": "read_by",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "gemini"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Fallback - Scan for Opt-Out Words",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.5,
      "position": [
        1320,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "intent",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Needs Owner Review"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "is_opt_out",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ /\\b(unsubscribe|opt ?out|stop emailing|remove me|do not contact|dont contact|take me off)\\b/i.test($('Normalize the Reply').item.json.reply_text) ? 'yes' : '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "summary",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Gemini was unavailable, so this reply has not been read. Open it yourself."
            },
            {
              "id": "a4",
              "name": "read_by",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "fallback-keyword-scan"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
